            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum(rate(latkit_redis_commands_total{proto=~\"$proto\",cmd=\"PING\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "refId": "A",
          "range": true,
          "instant": false,
          "legendFormat": "PING/s"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.99, sum by (le) (rate(latkit_redis_command_duration_seconds_bucket{proto=~\"$proto\",cmd=\"PING\"}[$__rate_interval])))",
          "refId": "B",
          "range": true,
          "instant": false,
          "legendFormat": "p99"
        }
      ],
      "description": "`PING` has a panel of its own rather than being folded into an `internal` bucket (РR15). In a typical deployment sidecars and connection pools make it up to half of all commands, and it is the single most useful measurement on this page: it does no work, so its p99 *is* the event loop's queueing delay. A `PING` p99 that rises while the command rate does not means one client's `KEYS *` is holding the server."
    },
